# .cursorrules — mirror of CLAUDE.md for Cursor users.
# The canonical source is CLAUDE.md. If the two drift, CLAUDE.md wins.

You are working in `good-vibes-only`, a Next.js 15 + TypeScript starter that doubles as a guide for AI-assisted development.

## Project shape

- `app/` — Next.js App Router pages, layouts, API routes, server actions
- `lib/` — Shared modules: env.ts, logger.ts, db.ts. Server-only by default.
- `tests/unit/` — Vitest specs.
- `tests/e2e/` — Playwright specs.
- `docs/` — The vibe-coding guide.
- `recipes/` — Opt-in add-ons (auth, db, payments, components).

## Always

- Read the target file and its neighbors before editing.
- Plan before coding anything beyond a one-line fix.
- Validate every external input with Zod (`safeParse`, branch on success).
- Read env via `lib/env.ts` — never `process.env` in app code.
- Default to server components. Use `"use client"` only when you need it.
- Use `import type` for types.
- Mark server-only modules with `import "server-only";` at the top.
- Log with structure: `logger.info({ userId }, "loaded user")`.
- Run `pnpm check` before claiming work done.

## Never

- No `any`. Use `unknown` and narrow.
- No `// @ts-ignore` without an inline reason.
- No `process.env.X` outside `lib/env.ts`.
- No new dependencies without justification in the PR description.
- No `console.log` in committed code — use `logger`.
- No premature abstractions for hypothetical callers.
- No husky, no pre-commit hooks, no CI workflows. Run `pnpm check` yourself before committing.

## Setup flow

If the user asks to "run setup" or "pick a component library":

1. Read `recipes/components/README.md`.
2. Ask the user to pick one (default Tailwind, shadcn/ui, MUI, Chakra, Mantine).
3. Apply the matching recipe in `recipes/components/<choice>.md`.
4. Commit with `chore: set up <library>`.

## Workflow

For any non-trivial change: state plan → implement small steps → add a test → `pnpm check` → update `docs/` if a convention changed.
